Çevirgen

Çevirgen is a modified version of CouchSubs.
Based on CouchSubs by Sinan Yorulmaz (https://github.com/yorulmazsinan/couchsubs),
version v0.1.0-beta.88, modified from 2026-11-23 onwards.

Çevirgen is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3, like
CouchSubs. The full history of changes is in this repository's git log; the
first commit is the unmodified upstream source.

Main changes (2026-11-23):
  - New name, logo and colors; separate data folder (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Cevirgen).
  - Upstream ads, shared-pool uploads, usage statistics and the upstream update
    channel are removed or disabled; Çevirgen sends nothing to CouchSubs servers.
  - Translation is placed above the whole stacked English subtitle block.
  - Button hints split by the text recognizer are recognised and not covered.
  - Late translations stay on screen for 0.5 s instead of 2-8 s.
  - New default look (above the subtitle, no background, bold, outlined text).
  - Optional black text outline on the TV.

Changes (2026-11-24):
  - Stacked subtitles: the Turkish of an older line stays above the new line while
    its English is still on screen, and leaves with it (TV app 1.0.1).
  - User corrections ("Düzelt") that win over packs, cache and engines.
  - User glossary with "keep" / "always translate as" rules.
  - Reading speed (characters per second) per line and session summary.
  - SRT export (Turkish and bilingual) from the subtitle history.
  - Shortcut (Ctrl+H) to hide/show subtitles without stopping translation.
  - Remote settings from Çevirgen's own server (cevirgen-api): bottom ad band, daily
    pop-up and announcements can change without an app update; cached for offline use.
  - Optional anonymous usage count (random install id, version, platform, playing)
    sent to Çevirgen's server every 5 minutes; can be turned off in Settings.
  - Updates come from Çevirgen's own GitHub releases (ozguradmin/cevirgen).
  - New Windows interface: graphite theme with one accent colour, embedded IBM Plex
    and Archivo Condensed fonts (SIL OFL 1.1), new top bar and sections, live screen
    with TV preview and transcript, "where do you play?" setup (PS5, Xbox, PC, other)
    and regrouped settings.

Changes (2026-11-24, interface polish):
  - One status colour model everywhere (green ready, amber waiting, red error,
    grey off); keyboard-only focus rings; calmer typography (monospace only for
    timecodes, numbers and keys).
  - Translation tab: engine list and setup first, optional blind comparison
    that runs only on request and only with ready engines; custom
    OpenAI-compatible endpoint engine (URL, model, optional key).
  - Live preview shows the real or last captured frame instead of a drawn
    placeholder scene.
  - Shorter setup (PS5 and Xbox 4 steps, PC 2 steps, other 3 steps).
  - Çevirgen server reached at its own domain with automatic fallback.
  - Free (OPUS-MT) engine: characters outside the model vocabulary no longer
    vanish ("coño", "Mañana", "mahkûm"); accented source letters are simplified
    before translation and restored afterwards; stricter sentence splitting
    (initialisms, ellipsis inside quotes); short lines translated with context
    keep their capital initial.
  - Turkish button and label texts in sentence case.
  - Live screen: one notice strip above the TV preview (most important notice
    first: blocking errors, then needed actions, then information); the game
    picker is a searchable grid of cover tiles (remote covers from Çevirgen's own
    config, user covers first); settings list shows version and project links;
    a calm, non-dismissible support line after the first 20 translated lines;
    anonymous count switch only in Settings.

